#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Curate autodev's own scoped RAG collection (``autodev-kb``) from source.

This is the curation pipeline the ratified identity/sandbox design calls for
(``autodev-service-identity-and-sandbox``): a SEPARATE Qdrant collection built
by curating a deliberate, named subset of source documents — not a copy of
points from any shared collection (``tzervas-dev-kb``, ``fleet-model-kb``,
``fleet-csd-kb``, ``fleet-gap-kb``, ``fleet-harness-kb``).

Scope (operator, 2026-09-07): the collection must be scoped to the tasks
autodev is actually working — the relevant repos, relevant official docs, and
the intended paradigms/patterns/tools. Explicitly NOT a copy of the big store.

**What is in MANIFEST and why**

Autodev's Forgejo collaborator grant covers exactly two repos —
``tzervas/CogSynDelta`` and ``tzervas/memory-gate`` — so the curated corpus
mirrors that write scope 1:1: knowledge about a repo autodev cannot touch is
not "relevant to the tasks being worked". Within each repo:

- CogSynDelta: ``AGENTS.md`` (conventions/paradigms/patterns/tools — the repo's
  own dev contract), every ``docs/adr/*.md`` (not ``archive/`` — superseded),
  the architecture/contract/spec docs under ``docs/design/`` (corpus contract,
  interconnect spec, licence verdicts, metrics methodology, model manifests,
  training stack, region taxonomy, training superset, visual ingest,
  completion plan, state-vs-plan), the decision/pre-registration documents
  under ``docs/design/evidence/**`` (``PREREG.md``, ``GO_KILL.md``,
  ``BATTERY-DEFECT.md``, ``README.md`` — every evidence dir's verdict, not its
  raw survey/analysis dumps), and ``program/REMAINING.md`` (the live task
  board — the single "what to work on" reference).
- memory-gate: ``README.md``, every ``docs/adr/*.md``, ``docs/security/*.md``,
  and the ``memory-lifecycle-contract`` spec + tasks.

**Deliberately excluded** (and why): ``docs/plain/``, ``docs/foundations/``,
``docs/technical/`` (reader-facing tracks for humans, not dev-loop material);
``docs/archive/``, ``docs/adr/archive/`` (superseded); the dataset-sourcing
catalogues (``DATASET-FACTORY-CATALOGUE*``, ``AUDIO-CORPUS-AUDIT``,
``REASON-CORPUS-CANDIDATES*`` — data-sourcing side, not architecture/code
material) and the raw ``ANALYSIS.md``/survey files under ``evidence/**``
(kept only the verdict files, to stay a decision corpus, not a data dump);
every OTHER repo in the fleet (fleet-ai-platform, gpu-pack, model-matrix,
dataset-factory, csd-autodev itself, ternary-track, mycelium, weird-paradigms,
...) — none of them are repos autodev can write to; the Obsidian vaults and
their Qdrant collections entirely (autodev does not touch Obsidian, per the
ratified design — RAG only); anything secrets-adjacent or topology-shaped
(none matched in the included set — checked by hand).

**Two-phase run, because embedding needs CUDA and curation should not**

    # Phase 1 (any host, no CUDA): chunk MANIFEST into a review-able JSONL.
    ./scripts/csd-autodev-rag-curate chunk --out /path/to/chunks.jsonl

    # Phase 2 (CUDA host only, e.g. host-gpu-c over an SSH reverse tunnel back
    # to the Qdrant host): embed and upsert.
    ./scripts/csd-autodev-rag-curate embed --in /path/to/chunks.jsonl \\
        --qdrant http://127.0.0.1:6333 --collection autodev-kb

Point ids are UUID5 of (repo, path, heading-index, content sha256) — re-running
phase 2 on an unchanged corpus is a no-op upsert; a changed file's old chunks
for that path are deleted first (``vault_path`` payload filter), matching the
fleet's established idempotent-reindex pattern.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import hashlib
import json
import os
import re
import sys
import uuid
from pathlib import Path

REPO_ROOT = Path(
    os.environ.get("AUTODEV_CURATE_ROOT", Path.home() / "code/personal/tzervas")
)

# Pinned per memory-gate ADR-0003 (docs/adr/0003-qdrant-qwen3-1024.md) and the
# fleet-wide Qdrant binding (ADR-0001 in fleet-ai-platform): Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B,
# exactly 1024-d, Cosine. Never mix a different model/dim into this collection.
EMBED_MODEL = "Qwen/Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B"
EMBED_REVISION = "97b0c614be4d77ee51c0cef4e5f07c00f9eb65b3"
EMBED_DIM = 1024
COLLECTION = "autodev-kb"

# (repo, relpath) — repo is the directory name under REPO_ROOT and the Forgejo
# repo name (tzervas/<repo>); relpath is repo-relative.
